WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
On January 1, 1996, the
United States banned leaded

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.890
gasoline for cars on the road.

3
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.820
A ban is one tool.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.130
A tax on each unit of
pollution is another.

5
00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:15.090
Or picture a factory
dumping waste into a river,

6
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.300
and a fish farm downstream
that loses money from it.

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.100
Who owns that river?

8
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.570
So should a government tax pollution,

9
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.170
ban it, or let the two sides bargain over

10
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.810
the right to pollute?

11
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.800
In this mission, you'll set
a pollution tax yourself

12
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.860
and watch what happens to output.

13
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.170
Then you'll sit the factory and
the fish farm down to bargain,

14
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.610
and see who ends up paying whom.

15
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.930
Your mission: figure out
what each tool does well,

16
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.840
and where each one falls short.
